in this episode of cloud performance  atlas I helped some middleware pros with  their BigTable performance will we  upgrade to the latest version of  Awesomeness stay tuned to find out for a  company like time sliders time series  data is the backbone of their business  model but lately it's been the bane of  their users their main product is a  performance instrumentation library the  developers can add to their mobile apps  to get runtime data from the field sadly  this process of building and displaying  performance tables in the report web  pages quickly became a bottleneck and a  less than ideal experience for the  majority of their clients thankfully we  didn't have to look too far to find the  problem time stamps see every 100  milliseconds or so their library would  log the battery status creating an entry  into a big table where the row key  consisted of the word battery plus a  timestamp now while this seems like a  straightforward implementation it runs  into a problem with hot spotting I see  when a row key for a time series  includes a timestamp then all of your  rights will target a single node it'll  fill that node and then move on to the  next node in the cluster filling that  node and so on this pattern creates  scenarios where performance suffers for  your application addressing this  problems means leveraging the concept of  field promotion ah--this trick involves  moving fields from the column data into  the row key to make writes  non-contiguous for example time sliders  ended up promoting the user ID value  from a column to an element of the row  key this change solved their hot  spotting issue because of the fact that  the identifier for users provided a more  uniform distribution of row keys  splitting rights across multiple nodes  in the cluster reducing hot spotting and  improving performance  now in case field promotion doesn't work  for you then check out the article  linked in the description below where we  cover a few other alternatives likewise  don't forget to subscribe to our YouTube  channel for more great cloud performance  Atlas content because when it comes to  performance every millisecond counts  [Music]
 

